# Deviations from PROTOCOL_SWE_SONNET.md (written before any agent ran)

DS1. The task text reaches each subagent through its first command (cat <folder>/task.md), not inside the first message:
the orchestrator does not paste 235 issue texts. This adds one request to every session, in ALONE, KIT and the eyes
alike, which pulls every factor toward 1.0. The report gives requests and dollars both as measured and with that first
read removed. The predictions are scored on the measured numbers.

DS2 (after the 2-agent pilot on django__django-10914, before the rest). After submit.sh, each subagent makes one more
request to hand back its reply (SubagentHandback). In the API harness, submit ends the session. Like DS1, this adds one
request to every session in every arm. The adjusted figures remove both the task read and the hand-back. The measured
figures keep them, and the predictions are scored on the measured figures. The pilot's two sessions ran exactly as
pre-registered and are kept as the first issue's results.
